{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Halt iterative training dynamically when validation performance ceases to improve to prevent overfitting."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPClassifier"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") and gradient boosted decision trees ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EarlyStopping"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally restoring optimal model weights."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Mechanics--State-Machine","type":"heading","text":"Mechanics & State Machine"},{"code":["Epoch Evaluation (Score S_t)","            │","            ▼"," Is (Best - S_t) > minDelta?","   ├── YES ──► Reset wait = 0, update bestScore = S_t, checkpoint weights","   └── NO  ──► Increment wait = wait + 1","                 │","            Is wait >= patience?","              ├── YES ──► shouldStop = true, restore best checkpoint weights","              └── NO  ──► Continue training"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Configuration-Parameters","type":"heading","text":"Configuration Parameters"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"patience","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Number of consecutive non-improving evaluations tolerated before triggering an early halt."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"minDelta","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Minimum absolute improvement required to qualify as progress."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"direction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".minimize"},{"text":" for loss functions (cross-entropy, MSE) or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".maximize"},{"text":" for scoring metrics (accuracy, R2, AUC).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"restoreBestWeights","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":", automatically restores the model parameters from the epoch that achieved ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bestScore"},{"text":", avoiding overfit tail iterations.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example-Usage","level":2,"text":"Example Usage"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Configure early stopping callback","let es = EarlyStopping(","    patience: 5,","    minDelta: 1e-4,","    direction: .minimize,","    restoreBestWeights: true",")","","\/\/ 2. Fit MLP with validation monitoring","let mlp = MLPClassifier(hiddenLayerSizes: [32, 16], maxIter: 200)","try await mlp.fit(","    features: X_train,","    targets: y_train,","    validationFeatures: X_val,","    validationTargets: y_val,","    earlyStopping: es",")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}],"title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control","roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML"]]},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedClassifiers","doc:\/